Of course! Creating a hamburger menu is a great way to save space and keep navigation compact, especially for mobile devices. Here's an example of how you can set up a simple hamburger menu with HTML and CSS:

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
 <meta charset="UTF-8">
 <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
 <style>
 body {
 font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
 }
 .navbar {
 display: flex;
 justify-content: space-between;
 align-items: center;
 padding: 1em;
 background-color: #333;
 color: white;
 }
 .nav-menu {
 display: none;
 flex-direction: column;
 position: absolute;
 top: 60px;
 left: 0;
 width: 100%;
 background-color: #333;
 }
 .nav-menu a {
 color: white;
 padding: 1em;
 text-decoration: none;
 text-align: center;
 }
 .nav-menu a:hover {
 background-color: #575757;
 }
 .hamburger {
 cursor: pointer;
 font-size: 1.5em;
 }
 @media (min-width: 600px) {
 .nav-menu {
 display: flex;
 flex-direction: row;
 position: static;
 }
 .hamburger {
 display: none;
 }
 }
 </style>
</head>
<body>
 <header class="navbar">
 <div class="logo">My Website</div>
 <div class="hamburger" onclick="toggleMenu()">☰</div>
 <nav class="nav-menu" id="navMenu">
 <a href="#home">Home</a>
 <a href="#about">About</a>
 <a href="#services">Services</a>
 <a href="#contact">Contact</a>
 </nav>
 </header>

 <script>
 function toggleMenu() {
 var menu = document.getElementById('navMenu');
 if (menu.style.display === 'flex') {
 menu.style.display = 'none';
 } else {
 menu.style.display = 'flex';
 }
 }
 </script>
</body>
</html>
```

### Explanation:
- **HTML Structure**: The navigation content is placed within a `nav` tag with class `nav-menu`. The `div` with class `hamburger` acts as the toggle button.
- **CSS**: The `.nav-menu` is hidden by default on smaller screens, and the `.hamburger` menu icon is displayed. On larger screens, `.nav-menu` is displayed as a horizontal menu and the `.hamburger` is hidden.
- **JavaScript**: A simple function to toggle the display of the menu when the hamburger icon is clicked.

This setup ensures that your navigation is accessible and user-friendly across devices. Let me know if you need further assistance!

